edit(coq,'CoQ occurs in analysed olive oils and animal tissues.', 'Measured olive-oil results were 56 ± 4 mg/L for seven commercial extra-virgin blends, 52 ± 17 mg/L for 79 fresh/fresh-frozen monocultivar samples, and 54 ± 10 mg/L for two refined-oil samples. These are sample-group measurements, not universal values; no density-based conversion to mg/100 g or native ubiquinol fraction is inferred. [5]\n\nSix named pistachio samples contained 10.21–42.16 µg/g CoQ10 by nano-liquid chromatography. This does not establish one value for all cultivars or roasted kernels. [7]\n\nCoQ occurs in analysed olive oils and animal tissues.')
edit(coq,'<SubstanceMatrix tag="CoQ10" />','<SubstanceMatrix tag="CoQ10" />\n\n[Electron Transport Chain Function](/docs/biological-targets/brs4/fm1/brs4-fm1-pm1-electron-transport-chain-function) describes its established electron-carrier role; [Mitochondrial Protection & Redox Integrity](/docs/biological-targets/brs4/fm2/brs4-fm2-pm5-mitochondrial-protection-redox-integrity) covers the existing redox relationship. [Coenzyme Q Biosynthesis & Pool Availability](/docs/biological-targets/brs4/fm1/brs4-fm1-pm10-coenzyme-q-biosynthesis-and-pool-availability) owns production and distribution. These biological relationships do not establish that ordinary food intake increases mitochondrial CoQ10 or improves clinical outcomes. [1–3]')
p=Path(coq);p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\n[7] Aydoğan et al. (2023). [Nano-Liquid Chromatography with a New Monolithic Column for the Analysis of Coenzyme Q10 in Pistachio Samples](/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#food_composition_cbbabe8383bc). Sample-specific food composition, not tissue delivery.\n')
p=Path('docs/foods/heart.md');s=p.read_text().replace('    notes: Beef heart tissue','    notes: Beef heart tissue\n    source_reference: \'#food-source-3\'').replace('    presence_status: presence_supported_amount_unavailable','    presence_status: presence_supported_amount_unavailable\n    source_reference: \'#food-source-3\'');s+='\n<span id="food-source-3" />\n\n[3] Mattila et al. (2000). [Comparison of in-line connected diode array and electrochemical detectors in the high-performance liquid chromatographic analysis of coenzymes Q9 and Q10 in food materials](/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#food_composition_d3a572997731). Primary analytical evidence for beef-heart occurrence; no preparation-specific quantity assigned.\n';p.write_text(s)
p=Path('docs/foods/early-harvest-olive-oil.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace("source_reference: '#food-source-2'","source_reference: '#food-source-3'");s+='\n<span id="food-source-3" />\n\n[3] Žmitek et al. (2014). [Factors Influencing the Contents of Coenzyme Q10 and Q9 in Olive Oils](/docs/papers/BRAIN-Diet-References#zmitek_factors_2014). Maturity studied in Istrska belica and Leccino; no universal early-harvest concentration.\n';p.write_text(s)
